From 60ec14f9acd82d64662127114ac1214a5352ddd5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 20:51:40 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 29/32] software_isp: debayer_egl: Add a noise reduction and
 sharpening pass

The software ISP outputs the demosaiced picture with neither noise
reduction nor sharpening: noisy at high gain, soft otherwise.

Add a second pass to the GPU debayer, run only while the IPA asks for
either: the debayer renders into an intermediate texture of the output
size, and a post-filter shader smooths the luma with an edge-preserving
(bilateral) 3x3 filter and sharpens it with an unsharp mask cored by
the noise level, then writes the output. Both work on the
gamma-encoded picture and change the luma only. The strengths come in
the debayer parameters (sharpen, denoise).

The output's colour order becomes a uniform rather than a define, so
the first pass can write RGB for the second.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
